nvk-build-fixes.patch: build fixes for a clean build of Mesa 17ca6174 +
nvk/nvk-macos.patch, applied by nvk/pascal/scripts/prepare-mesa.sh after
nvk-pascal.patch. Found by the first from-scratch builds (macOS cross build
and Linux native build, 2026-11-08; nvk/pascal/CROSS-BUILD.md).

1. nv_push.h is also compiled as OpenCL C by mesa_clc (nvk/cl/
   nvk_copy_indirect.cl includes it). OpenCL C has no fprintf/stderr, so the
   "empty push method header" warning nvk-macos.patch added must be left
   out of that build; otherwise nvkcl.spv fails to compile on every
   platform. The C build is unchanged.

The NVRM backend's three Kepler class headers (class/cla0c0.h, cla197.h,
cla1c0.h), which open-gpu-kernel-modules 615.78.08 no longer ships, are
fetched by prepare-mesa.sh from 570.86.16 instead of being carried here.

diff -ruN a/src/nouveau/headers/nv_push.h b/src/nouveau/headers/nv_push.h
--- a/src/nouveau/headers/nv_push.h
+++ b/src/nouveau/headers/nv_push.h
@@ -132,6 +132,7 @@
     * vk_meta_draw_volume) reached here with an empty method and aborted Chess,
     * mediaanalysisd and several video apps.  Warn once and continue, as the
     * stale rasterization-samples assert in nvk_cmd_draw.c was downgraded. */
+#ifndef __OPENCL_VERSION__ /* nv_push.h is also compiled as OpenCL C (nvk/cl), which has no stdio */
    if (last_count == 0) {
       static int warned;
       if (!warned) {
@@ -139,6 +140,7 @@
          fprintf(stderr, "nvk: empty push method header (count 0); continuing\n");
       }
    }
+#endif
 }

 static inline void
